    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d709">

                <pb facs="1042" n="1014" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v03/pg1014"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">310.2/8–2554: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Cambodia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Goodman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Department of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Phnom Penh</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1954-08-25T18:00:00+07:00">August 25, 1954—6
                            p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>86. By confidential note Foreign Ministry has informed Embassy Cambodian
                    Government has accepted offer Australian Government to raise question Cambodian
                    membership UN at next General Assembly session.
                    Ministry asks that US support candidacy.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d709-f1"/></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Goodman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d709-f1" n="1" xml:id="d709-f1-content">
                <p>The Department of State replied in telegram 42, Sept. 2, 1954, 12:06 p.m.: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“US continues favor Cambodia’s admission UN your 86 and will support such proposal at forthcoming
                                UNGA.” (310.2/8–2554)</p>
                    </quote></p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
